### Compound-Assignment Audit (§2)

Searched for all occurrences of `+= (int)(`, `-= (int)(`, `+= (int)`, `-= (int)` across `Craft.java`:

| # | Line | Java Expression | Class. | Reasoning & Discriminating Input Shape | Confidence |
|---|---|---|:---:|---|:---:|
| 1 | 77 | `conto.zy -= (int)(5.0f * conto.m.cs.getcos(conto.xy));` | **Case A** | `conto.zy` is `int`, `5.0f * getcos(...)` is `float`. Java bytecode widens LHS to float (`i2f`), subtracts float, and narrows once (`f2i`). Discriminator: `conto.zy` positive (e.g. 5) with fractional subtrahend (e.g. 0.6) yields 4 under Case A vs 5 under Case B. | **HIGH** |
| 2 | 78 | `conto.xz += (int)(byte0 * 3 * conto.m.cs.getsin(conto.xy));` | **Case A** | LHS is `int`, `byte0 * 3 * getsin(...)` is `float`. LHS widened (`i2f`), float addition, truncated at end (`f2i`). Discriminator: positive accumulator with negative fractional step. | **HIGH** |
| 3 | 81 | `conto.zy += (int)(5.0f * conto.m.cs.getcos(conto.xy));` | **Case A** | Same structure as Site 1 with addition. LHS widened (`i2f`), float add, narrowed (`f2i`). Discriminator: negative accumulator with positive fractional step. | **HIGH** |
| 4 | 82 | `conto.xz -= (int)(byte0 * 3 * conto.m.cs.getsin(conto.xy));` | **Case A** | Same structure as Site 2 with subtraction. LHS widened (`i2f`), float sub, narrowed (`f2i`). | **HIGH** |
| 5 | 124 | `conto.zy += (int)(5.0f * conto.m.cs.getcos(conto.xy));` | **Case A** | Same structure as Site 3. LHS widened (`i2f`), float add, narrowed (`f2i`). | **HIGH** |
| 6 | 154 | `conto.xz += (int)(Math.random() * (this.speed / 10.0f) - this.speed / 20.0f);` | **Case A** | LHS is `int`, RHS is `double`. LHS widened (`i2d`), double add, narrowed (`d2i`). Downstream of random, but structured as Case A. | **HIGH** |
| 7 | 155 | `conto.zy += (int)(Math.random() * (this.speed / 10.0f) - this.speed / 20.0f);` | **Case A** | Same structure as Site 6. LHS widened (`i2d`), double add, narrowed (`d2i`). | **HIGH** |
| 8 | 171 | `conto.y -= (int)this.lift;` | **Case B** | `this.lift` is `double`. Notice Procyon emits `(int)this.lift` without surrounding expression parentheses (explicit cast on simple field read). In bytecode, `d2i` truncates `lift` first, then integer subtracts `isub` from `conto.y`. Discriminator: `lift = 0.5`, `conto.y = 100` — Case B does not change `y` (100 - 0 = 100), whereas Case A would step `y` to 99 every tick. | **HIGH** |
| 9 | 316 | `lx[n2] -= (int)(this.lspeed[l3] * (conto.m.cs.getsin(this.lxz[l3]) * conto.m.cs.getcos(this.lzy[l3])));` | **Case A** | `lx[n2]` is `int` in `int[]`, RHS is float32 expression (`lspeed * (sin * cos)`). LHS widened (`i2f`), float sub, stored via `iastore` with `f2i`. Discriminator: positive coordinate with fractional step. | **HIGH** |
| 10 | 319 | `lz[n3] += (int)(this.lspeed[l3] * (conto.m.cs.getcos(this.lxz[l3]) * conto.m.cs.getcos(this.lzy[l3])));` | **Case A** | Same as Site 9 with addition. LHS widened (`i2f`), float add, stored via `iastore` with `f2i`. | **HIGH** |
| 11 | 322 | `ly[n4] -= (int)(this.lspeed[l3] * conto.m.cs.getsin(this.lzy[l3]));` | **Case A** | Same as Site 9 with single sine term. LHS widened (`i2f`), float sub, narrowed (`f2i`). | **HIGH** |
| 12 | 340 | `conto.x -= (int)(this.speed * (conto.m.cs.getsin(conto.xz) * conto.m.cs.getcos(conto.zy)));` | **Case A** | LHS is `int`, RHS is float32 speed * trig. LHS widened (`i2f`), float sub, narrowed (`f2i`). Discriminator: accumulator positive, fractional step negative. | **HIGH** |
| 13 | 341 | `conto.z += (int)(this.speed * (conto.m.cs.getcos(conto.xz) * conto.m.cs.getcos(conto.zy)));` | **Case A** | Same as Site 12 with addition. LHS widened (`i2f`), float add, narrowed (`f2i`). | **HIGH** |
